WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.050
Proteins are everywhere in our bodies,
and they can do lots of amazing things.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.310
Like tools, the shape of the protein is
very important. For example, scissors

3
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.620
have multiple blades that help it cut
things, while screwdrivers have a

4
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.010
shaped end that allow it to fit into a
screw. Without the proper shape, the

5
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:22.260
protein would not be able to perform
its job. Proteins don't start out,

6
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:26.240
though, in their final shape. To become
the proper shape, proteins need to go

7
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.150
through a process called protein
folding.

8
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.820
Proteins are made up of building blocks
called amino acids. These amino acids

9
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.560
are placed into chains, known as
polypeptides.

10
00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.500
To become the final protein, the
polypeptide needs to fold into its

11
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.710
proper shape. But how do proteins know
what shape to fold into? Amino acids in

12
00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:49.750
a polypeptide follow a wide variety of
rules to fold into the final protein.

13
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.950
For example, some amino acids love
water, while others dislike water,

14
00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:59.860
which could affect where those amino
acids are placed in the protein. Other

15
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.290
amino acids enjoy being close to each
other and can form bonds so that they

16
00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:07.430
stay next to each other in the final
protein. However, protein folding is

17
00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.560
incredibly complex, and there are many
other rules to help ensure that

18
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.850
proteins fold properly.

19
00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:16.660
Because proteins are everywhere in our
body and perform many jobs, it is

20
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.820
important that they fold into the
proper shape. If proteins don't have

21
00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.440
the right shape, that can cause
problems, like clumping together. These

22
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:28.310
problem proteins can play a role in
diseases, like Alzheimer's and mad cow

23
00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:32.950
disease. Luckily, our body has a number
of ways to deal with misfolded proteins.

24
00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.340
They can get rid of the problem
proteins or use proteins, called

25
00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.340
chaperones, to help fix and refold
proteins into the proper shape. We're

26
00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.670
still learning so much about the exact
rules for how proteins fold and how the

27
00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:50.250
shape of a protein can teach us about
the job it performs. Understanding both

28
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:54.250
of these can help us understand not
only how proteins work, but how to

29
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:57.120
treat diseases related to problems of
protein folding

